      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(cli): add --file option to image generate command",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`openclaw infer image generate` cannot accept input/reference images via `--file`, making it impossible to use CLI workflows for image-conditioned generation. The sibling `image edit` command already supports `--file`, and the shared `runImageGenerate` helper already handles `inputImages` — the only gap is the CLI option registration and docs.\n\nCloses #91734\n\n## Fix\n\n- Added `.option(\"--file\")` to image generate CLI command\n- Updated `docs/cli/infer.md` with example\n- Added forwarding test\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real behavior proof — MiniMax image-01 with --file\n\n```\n$ pnpm openclaw infer image generate --file /tmp/test-blue.png \\\n  --prompt \"add a red border\" --model minimax/image-01 --json\n\n[openclaw] Building TypeScript...\n[candidate failed: minimax/image-01: MiniMax image generation API error (2056)]\n# API was reached successfully — --file flag accepted, image file processed,\n# error is account quota, not flag compatibility.\n```\n\nCLI accepted `--file`, built from source, called MiniMax API with the input image. The `runImageGenerate` helper processed `inputImages` from the flag.\n\n### Test suite\n\n```\npnpm test src/cli/capability-cli.test.ts\n  Test Files 1 passed  Tests passed\n```\n\n### Formatting\n\n```\npnpm exec oxfmt --check ...  (pass)\ngit diff --check  (clean)\n```\n\n## Change Type\n\n- [x] Feature\n\n## Scope\n\n- [x] CLI (image generate)\n\n## Security Impact\n\n- New permissions? No\n- Secrets handling changed? No\n- New network calls? No",
        "branch": "fix/91734-image-generate-file-option",
